// Debug signing.
//
// The default is ad-hoc ("-") so a fresh clone builds with no certificates at all.
// Ad-hoc signing has no certificate chain to anchor to, so the binary's designated
// requirement degrades to a literal `cdhash H"..."` — a hash of the executable that
// changes on every build. Keychain ACLs identify an app by that requirement, so each
// rebuild reads as a different app and macOS re-asks for the login keychain password;
// "Always Allow" only ever whitelists the build you clicked it on.
//
// A maintainer who holds a signing certificate can escape that by creating
// `macOS/Signing.local.xcconfig`, which is gitignored and included below when it
// exists. Its requirement anchors to the certificate and the bundle identifier
// instead of the executable's bytes, so it survives rebuilds and one "Always Allow"
// holds. The exact settings are in docs/RELEASING.md — signing metadata is spelled
// out only in the few files the leak scanner allows it in, and this is not one.

CODE_SIGN_IDENTITY = -

#include? "Signing.local.xcconfig"
